v1.1 - Apr 2026
Overshoots: rounded characters such as O, U, c, e are usually larger vertically than square or flat ones such as A, M, x, z. The difference (the "overshoot") is bigger in FreeSans than in most other fonts.
FreeSans: typical overshoot is 23 below baseline, 12 above cap height (729), 9-15 above x height. Kurinto Aria, IBM Plex Sans, and several others have overshoots closer to 10 (proportionally, in the case of fonts with em = 2048).
Overshoots have been reduced to 10 (or slightly less, in a few cases), for Latin (incl supplemental & derived), Greek, Cyrillic.
Modified l (with hook) now has overshoot = 5 below baseline.
Numerals: heights were lower than standard cap height. Adjusted flat numeral tops to 712, rounded to 722; overshoot below baseline is now 10.
Edited left and right bearings in some Greek and Cyrillic characters. Some Greek and Cyrillic capital letters were not copies of the appropriate Latin characters. Changed this where possible.

Added these to all four fonts, all with width 1000:
U+23AF horizontal line extension (with same vertical position as arrows).
This extends 25 to left & right of the box, so that typical letter-spacing will produce overlap with adjacent arrows.
U+27F5 long leftward arrow (also extends 25 to right of box)
U+27F6 long rightward arrow (also extends 25 to left of box)

***************************
v1.01 - Feb-Mar 2026
Adjustments/edits:
Bearings on I (50 left, 50 right) and l (60, 30)
Other characters based on I and l (diacritics, l with slash, etc.)
Added hooks to fl and ffl ligatures (U+FB02, U+FB04)
Broadened Roman numerals containing I (2160-216b) to keep 20 space between I characters
Period (".", U+002E) - width is now the same as comma, 1/2 that of numerals
Ä, Ë, Ï, Ü: aligned vertical spacing of dieresis
ν (Greek nu, U+03BD) removed reference to Latin v; made right side of letter curved (like that in Kurinto Aria)
+, − (minus, U+2212), ×, ÷ aligned them all vertically; made a few other minor edits

***************************
v1 - Jan 2026
Started with FreeSans .sfd files (version of 2012-05-03).
Changed I and l only.
Added serifs to I:
regular, 82 w x 82 h
bold, 100 w x 125 h
Added hook to l:
regular, 72 w x 72 h hook, with r = 72 curve
bold, 100 w x 120 h hook, with r = 120 curve

